    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Practical everyday tips"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "Start the day with a balanced breakfast.",
        "Avoid repeated sugary snacking.",
        "Include a variety of vegetables every day.",
        "Eat walnuts or almonds regularly.",
        "Walk at least thirty minutes a day.",
        "Eat your meals in a calm setting.",
        "Keep regular sleep hours."
      ],
      "levels": [
        0,
        0,
        0,
        0,
        0,
        0,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "These simple habits can gradually improve mental energy and emotional well-being."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "text": "Conclusion"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Diet influences far more than weight or cardiovascular health. It plays an active part in brain function, in the production of neurotransmitters and in emotional balance. Appropriate nutrition helps support concentration, motivation, resilience to stress and quality of life."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "According to the Family Clinic approach, taking care of one's diet is one of the most natural and accessible ways to promote lasting psychological well-being."
    },
